      [32m✔[39m treatments: an array, one slot per item, the stored records, no per-item results
      [32m✔[39m entries: an array, one slot per item, the stored records, no per-item results
      [32m✔[39m devicestatus: an array, one slot per item, the stored records, no per-item results
      [32m✔[39m profile: an array, one slot per item, the stored records, no per-item results
      [32m✔[39m a non-hex _id still refuses the whole devicestatus batch with 400 (R2 per item is opt-in)
      [32m✔[39m a profile re-send that needs api:profile:update still refuses the whole batch with 401 (decision (iii))
    NightscoutKit (Loop): 200, as many slots as sent, a string _id on every slot not refused
      [32m✔[39m under WRITE_IDENTIFIER=strict, a refused item keeps its slot: three sent, three answered
      [32m✔[39m entries and device status: as many slots as sent, each with a string _id
      [32m✔[39m a treatment with preBolus: one slot per sent item, no derived record in the reply (BF-219)
    xdripswift and nightscout-connect: each slot echoes its own item
      [32m✔[39m treatments: created_at, eventType and carbs echoed slot by slot
      [32m✔[39m entries: dateString echoed, and the newest date in the reply is the newest sent (the connect bookmark)
      [32m✔[39m treatments with preBolus: the newest created_at in the reply is the newest sent
    R3: status
      [32m✔[39m a partly refused batch answers 200; every item refused answers 400; every item a taken _id answers 200
      [32m✔[39m opt-in: partly refused 200; every item refused 400 with the slots
    the opt-in (decision (ii)): Nightscout-Write-Results: items
      [32m✔[39m answers { items, documents }: one item per submitted index, in order, with outcomes
      [32m✔[39m ?results=items is the same opt-in; any other value is refused 400 before anything is written
      [32m✔[39m R2: a non-hex _id refuses its item, the rest stored
      [32m✔[39m (iii): a profile re-send needing api:profile:update is refused 403 in its slot, the new profiles stored
      [32m✔[39m (vi): a device status re-sent by its stored _id is acknowledged, counted, nothing written
      [32m✔[39m (vi): a treatment re-sent with a deleted record's identifier is acknowledged and stays deleted
      [32m✔[39m WRITE_VALIDATION=reject: every Temporary Target refused keeps its slots under the opt-in (400 with the slots)

