  PostgreSQL entries write differential (requires disposable PostgreSQL and MongoDB)
    - inserts JSON documents with preserved stored kind and normalizes only the input requested
    - matches identifier preference, exact storedId and both kinds, with accurate no-op counts
    - updates and deletes strict filter matches without changing unrelated fields or tenant B
    - deletes the same single record as MongoDB before falling back to ObjectId then string
    - refuses data-dependent identifier sorting before changing any matching record
    - rolls back failed operations, refuses unbound writes and identifies only known duplicate keys
    - merges repeated upserts in order, preserving omitted fields, insert-only values and typed identity
    - replaces without retaining omitted fields, preserves identity, and does not resurrect without upsert
    - uses JSONB value equality for order-only replacement counts when _id is present
    - refuses over-cap update and delete matches without changing any rows
    - locks overlapping multi-row updates in the same stable order
    - updates/removes every displayed form, scopes resolved identities, and reports over-cap resolution
    - exposes ordered prefixes and unordered continuation after duplicate _id, with a usable transaction
    - recovers an identifier conflict using a savepoint so a caller can rematch only that operation
    - does not translate or retry an unrelated unique constraint
    - runs shared v3 matching and create/resend/PUT/PATCH/delete rules with the same named results and events
    - publishes the shared intent event only after commit; rollback and nested boundaries publish nothing
    - settles an actual concurrent identifier insert as one v3 resend after recovering the failed SQL statement
    - serializes competing patches without losing fields
    - allows tenant B to write its own overlapping ids without changing tenant A

  operator PostgreSQL migrations (disposable Docker) [pending opt-in: NS_MIGRATION_DOCKER_TEST=1]
    - status/check are read-only even before the namespace and ledger exist
