    - applies the reviewed entries candidate with typed v3 fields, tenant identity and forced RLS
    - does not silently inherit ambient application or PG connection configuration
    - serializes overlapping runners, commits exactly once and accepts current schema
    - has a bounded lock wait and leaves the lock holder unaffected
    - rolls failed DDL and ledger back together and resumes without rewriting prior history
    - refuses multi-statement transaction escape and rolls back its first statement
    - refuses applied checksum drift and unknown history on both inspection and mutation
    - refuses non-prefix ledger history instead of applying migrations out of order
