    - serializes competing inserts to exactly one immutable reference
    - commits audit before provider work even when an unrelated caller transaction rolls back
    - refuses extra audit fields instead of persisting secret payloads
    - enforces RLS against omitted predicates, unbound reads and foreign-tenant inserts
    - makes audit append-only and unreadable to the application role
    - uses a separate ciphertext-only maintenance role with compare-and-swap protection
    - refuses unsafe startup roles and missing schemas without migrating
    - red control: disabling actual RLS exposes foreign rows to omitted-predicate SQL
    - fails before decryption when the audit insert is refused
    - survives a database restart and preserves committed audit/reference records
    - restores ciphertext, audit and required Vault key versions from synthetic backups
    - persists real Vault ciphertext and retries scoped rewrap across races, failures and SIGKILL

